(footprint "DWM3001C_PLACEHOLDER"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "uwb_rescue_locator_lib_builder")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "PLACEHOLDER footprint for Qorvo/Decawave DWM3001C fully integrated UWB transceiver module (DW3110 + nRF52833 + LIS2DH12 + on-module antenna), 48-pin castellated LGA, body 19.13x27.1x3.2mm. Pin count and edge assignment are real/confirmed against Qorvo DWM3001C Data Sheet Rev B May 2022 Figure 1 'DWM3001C Pin Diagram' (17 pads left edge pins 1-17 top-to-bottom, 14 pads bottom edge pins 18-31 left-to-right, 17 pads right edge pins 32-48 bottom-to-top, none on the top edge -- that edge carries the module's own UWB antenna). Body/land envelope (19.13x27.1mm body, 19.10x27.10mm land, 16.27mm inner column gap, 0.75mm side pad height, 17.77mm side column span, 1.00mm bottom-row pitch, 1.15mm bottom pad length) are read directly off Figure 4 and Figure 5. Two things did NOT cleanly resolve and are ESTIMATES: (1) the side column pitch back-derives to 1.06375mm from the 17.77mm span, which is not a round number and is unlikely to be Qorvo's intent; (2) Figure 5's '3.10' annotation implies the bottom pad row is offset toward the right rather than centred, and its individual pad width is not dimensioned at all -- 0.60mm centred is assumed here. Verify both against Qorvo DWM3001C Data Sheet Rev B, Section 8.2 Figure 5 'Module Land Pattern' before fabrication. Flagged PLACEHOLDER per project convention, same as DWM3000_PLACEHOLDER.")
	(tags "Qorvo Decawave DWM3001C UWB nRF52833 module castellated PLACEHOLDER")
